  "schema_version": "formalization-faithfulness-1",
  "role": "adjudicator",
  "task_id": "LEV-CH01-SOURCE-TERMS-INTERPRETED-PRODUCTION-20260908",
  "trigger": [
    "direct judge requested adjudication",
    "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
    "direct judge classification is undetermined",
    "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
    "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D001 unclear",
    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
    "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
    "direct judge left implication lean_implies_source unclear",
    "direct judge left implication source_implies_lean unclear",
    "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
    "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The substantive issue is correspondence of the production-density domains, not the validity of the balance algebra. Independent inspection confirms that the recorded convention does not explicitly settle joint versus iterated local integrability or exceptional-time representatives. Adjudication cannot supply an additional convention as though it were already recorded.",
      "primary_evidence": "The recorded Q6 interpretation selects signed locally integrable production densities. D001 instead explicitly lists spatial slice integrability at every time and temporal integrability of signed spatial production integrals. Printed page 4 supplies no production function space."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The blind translation accurately reconstructs the relevant Lean conditions and conclusions. Its warning about absent joint integrability is supported by the declaration body, so this is not a translation error.",
      "primary_evidence": "LocalDef001 in the blind dossier and IsRectangleBalanceLawSolution in the direct dossier have the same five conditions. The blind translation preserves their quantifiers, signed iterated integrals, and assumed rectangle identity."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined because the exact interpreted source domain remains unspecified at the disputed analytic boundary. Correct identities on the Lean domain do not establish that the domain matches the selected source interpretation.",
      "primary_evidence": "Methodology section 2 requires applicability to be assessed and prohibits treating additional hypotheses or missing cases as stronger results. D001 imposes an everywhere-in-time spatial production integrability condition not explicitly selected by Q6."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined independently of agreement with the direct judge. The reconstructed proposition leaves the same unresolved correspondence between the selected density class and the explicit slice conditions.",
      "primary_evidence": "The translation's hypotheses require production slices to be integrable for every time, while its restrictions expressly distinguish these assumptions from joint space-time integrability. Q6 does not identify the two."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D001 unclear",
      "resolution": "D001's declaration meaning is resolved: it requires four integrability families and sourced balance on every oriented rectangle. It neither states joint measurability nor requires temporal integration of the spatial integral of the absolute production density. Only its correspondence to Q6 remains unclear. D002 shares its first two integrability families, so under h failure of D002 detects a failed homogeneous balance identity rather than failed integrability.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001's body contains IntervalIntegrable for q spatial slices, flux temporal slices, production spatial slices, and temporal functions τ ↦ ∫ x in a..b, production x τ, followed by the rectangle identity. D002 contains the first two families and the homogeneous identity. D102 defines one-variable interval integrability."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "The hypothesis correspondence remains unclear. Ordinary joint local integrability does not require every exceptional-time spatial slice to be integrable. A precise representative convention could reconcile this, but none is supplied. The almost-everywhere mass derivative itself introduces no missing classical spatial smoothness assumption.",
      "primary_evidence": "For q=0 and speed=0, let production(x,t) equal 1/|x| when t=0 and 0<|x|<1, and zero otherwise, in the sole coordinate. This measurable field is zero almost everywhere in space-time and jointly locally integrable, but its t=0 spatial slice is not integrable near zero, violating D001. Printed pages 4–5 distinguish classical PDE regularity from integral conservation."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The potential restriction on exceptional-time representatives is substantive and cannot be called genuine strength. Conversely, control of signed spatial aggregates cannot simply be identified with joint absolute integrability. No faithful-stronger classification is established.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 quantifies its spatial production integrability clause over every t and integrates production before imposing temporal integrability. It contains no condition integrating |production| over space and time. Q6 uses locally integrable densities without specifying this alternative domain."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation correctly preserves the disputed hypotheses. The exceptional-time example establishes a real distinction from an unrestricted joint-L1_loc representative convention, although it is not a counterexample to the Lean theorem.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind hypotheses say every a,b,t for spatial production integrability. The field supported at t=0 described above belongs to the joint-L1_loc class but fails precisely this condition. The theorem is conditional on that condition."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "Exclusion of singular production measures matches the recorded choice. That exclusion alone does not determine which function representatives and integrability conditions are intended. The remaining specialization/generalization question therefore stays unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target takes production : Real → Real → Fin 1 → Real, not a measure. Q6 excludes general singular production measures but does not specify joint versus iterated integrability or exceptional-slice treatment."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication lean_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation, source-term necessity is established on the common admitted balance-law domain: a failure of homogeneous conservation forces nonzero integrated production on some rectangle. Coverage of the entire selected density domain remains unclear.",
      "primary_evidence": "The fourth target conjunct states ¬IsRectangleConservationLawSolution q flux ↔ ∃a b s t, P_ab(s,t)≠0. Printed page 4 distinguishes endpoint transport from contaminant nonconservation requiring source terms. D001's every-time production slice condition creates the unresolved applicability boundary."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication source_implies_lean unclear",
      "resolution": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation, every target conclusion is justified on the common domain. However, this does not identify the exact universal Lean domain with the selected density class. The full semantic implication remains unclear, rather than being inferred merely because the Lean conclusions follow mathematically from h.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 gives ΔM=F+P, hence P=ΔM−F and homogeneous balance iff all P vanish. For fixed a,b, its temporal integrability clauses make B_ab+R_ab locally integrable and its balance identity represents mass as an indefinite integral plus a constant, yielding the stated almost-everywhere derivative."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation, the translation expresses the intended necessity on its assumed solution domain. The same unresolved representative and integrability boundary prevents certification for every case admitted by the selected interpretation.",
      "primary_evidence": "The translation's Q_ab, B_ab, and P_ab retain mass, endpoint exchange, and internal production separately. Its every-time spatial production hypothesis agrees exactly with D001 and is not expressly fixed by Q6."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation, the translation's algebraic and almost-everywhere conclusions follow on the common domain. The translation adds no discrepancy beyond the unresolved domain correspondence already found in the declarations.",
      "primary_evidence": "The direct and blind target types agree after replacing the two local predicate names. Both have ∀a b, almost every t for HasDerivAt of interval mass, not a common exceptional set for every interval or a classical pointwise PDE."
    },
    {
      "item": "Remaining dependency semantics, boundary cases, and nonvacuity",
      "resolution": "The supplied declarations support ordinary scalar arithmetic, oriented Lebesgue interval integrals, genuine derivative existence, and per-interval null exceptional sets. Fin 1 is nonempty and represents one scalar. Zero speed and reversed or coincident endpoints cause no semantic defect. Nonzero production cases satisfy h, so repeating h as the first conjunct does not make the entire result vacuous.",
      "primary_evidence": "D004, D017, and the Pi arithmetic declarations give coordinatewise real multiplication, addition, and subtraction. D095 supplies oriented integrals. The native supplement explicitly identifies Real.measureSpace.volume with the identity Stieltjes measure and gives volume(Ioc a b)=ENNReal.ofReal(b−a). D014, D021, and D032 specify genuine derivatives almost everywhere. Taking q(x,t)(0)=exp(t) and production(x,t)(0)=exp(t) satisfies all D001 conditions for any constant speed, with P_ab(s,t)=(b−a)(exp(t)−exp(s)), nonzero for a<b and s<t."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation, the Lean theorem correctly gives source-term necessity, the transport-adjusted mass defect, and the per-fixed-interval almost-everywhere mass-rate identity for fields satisfying D001. The full implication remains unclear because the selected locally integrable density class does not explicitly require every-time spatial production integrability or specify representatives satisfying it. The printed source does not settle that boundary."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation, rectangle balance and the explicit temporal integrability conditions justify all target conclusions on the common domain. The residual identity and biconditionals follow by cancellation, and interval mass has an indefinite-integral representation giving its derivative almost everywhere. Nevertheless, the selected density class has not been identified with D001's universal slice-and-aggregate domain. Mathematical validity of the conditional theorem alone does not certify this semantic implication for the exact selected claim."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "Whether Q6's locally integrable production densities means joint space-time L1_loc, the exact iterated conditions of D001, or joint local integrability together with additional slice conditions.",
    "Whether production is compared as a fixed pointwise representative or modulo space-time null sets, and whether exceptional-time slices may be replaced before applying the theorem.",
    "The printed passage itself leaves the production function space, source equation, and nonzero criterion unspecified; the recorded interpretation must remain separate from the book's assertions."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unresolved-effective-domain",
      "evidence": "D001 explicitly requires spatial production integrability at every time and temporal integrability of signed spatial aggregates. Q6 selects locally integrable production densities without fixing these conditions or representative treatment. A density supported at t=0 with spatial slice 1/|x| near zero is jointly locally integrable as a space-time field but fails D001.",
      "impact": "The distinction affects applicability and prevents acceptance. It is not a counterexample to the conditional Lean identities and does not justify classifying the theorem as stronger."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "interpretation-qualified-correspondence",
      "evidence": "Printed page 4 gives f(q)=ūq, endpoint mass exchange, and the conditional necessity of source terms. The target additionally assumes a sourced rectangle model and characterizes production through integrated balances, with a per-interval almost-everywhere derivative.",
      "impact": "These conclusions are coherent within the recorded mathematical interpretation. Any eventual acceptance must explicitly retain that qualification and cannot attribute its analytic conventions or biconditionals to the printed passage."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Independent inspection of the attached primary-source pages and inline declarations confirms the scalar flux, endpoint signs, distinction between transport and internal production, quantifier scope, and nonvacuity. The native declaration supplement supports the real-volume interpretation through explicit measure identities, not merely provenance hashes. The blind translation preserves the target's substantive semantics. The unresolved issue is the precise meaning of the selected production-density domain; neither the source nor the recorded convention resolves its relationship to D001's everywhere-slice and iterated-integral conditions. Consequently both full semantic implications remain unclear, consistently yielding undetermined and accepted=false. No tools were used, and no hashes were independently recomputed."
}
